  <strong>Gap:</strong> Only 4 of ~20 works-grid projects have MDX case studies.
  Others are outbound-only and not sitemap detail pages.
</div>

<h2>6. Dynamic Blog Posts (/blog/[slug])</h2>

<p><strong>Content:</strong> <code>content/blogs/*.mdx</code><br>
<strong>Helpers:</strong> <code>blog.ts</code>, <code>blog-seo.ts</code><br>
<strong>JSON-LD:</strong> Article schema</p>

<h3>Published posts (2)</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Slug</th><th>Title</th><th>Date</th><th>Image</th></tr>
  <tr><td>integrating-plaid-in-production</td><td>How I Learned Plaid While Building a Finance Application</td><td>June 25, 2026</td><td>/plaid.png</td></tr>
  <tr><td>http-query-method-explained-why-get-and-post-arent-always-enough</td><td>Why GET and POST Aren't Always Enough…</td><td>July 8, 2026</td><td>/httpquery.png</td></tr>
</table>

<p>Drafts with <code>published: false</code> are excluded from listing, indexing, and sitemap.</p>

<h2>7. Sitemap</h2>

<p><strong>URL:</strong> https://kunalkhandelwal.dev/sitemap.xml<br>
<strong>File:</strong> <code>src/app/sitemap.ts</code></p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Static (6):</strong> /, /works, /blog, /about, /credentials, /contact</li>
  <li><strong>Projects:</strong> all content/projects/*.mdx → /works/{slug}</li>
  <li><strong>Blogs:</strong> published content/blogs/*.mdx → /blog/{slug}</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Current size:</strong> 6 static + 4 projects + 2 blogs = <strong>12 URLs</strong></p>

<p><strong>Safeguards:</strong> no /works/undefined; drafts excluded; lastModified from file mtime.</p>

<h2>8. Robots.txt</h2>

<p><strong>URL:</strong> https://kunalkhandelwal.dev/robots.txt</p>
<pre>User-agent: *
Allow: /
Disallow: /api/
Disallow: /_next/

Sitemap: https://kunalkhandelwal.dev/sitemap.xml</pre>

<h2>9. Structured Data (JSON-LD)</h2>

<table>
  <tr><th>Schema</th><th>Where</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Person</td><td>Root layout</td><td>Identity, jobTitle, sameAs, knowsAbout</td></tr>
  <tr><td>WebSite</td><td>Root layout</td><td>Site entity linked to Person via @id</td></tr>
  <tr><td>CreativeWork</td><td>Project pages</td><td>Case study context</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Article</td><td>Blog pages</td><td>Headline, dates, author</td></tr>
</table>

<p><strong>Recommended next:</strong> BreadcrumbList on detail pages; ItemList on /works and /blog.</p>

<h2>10. Analytics (SEO-adjacent)</h2>

<table>
  <tr><th>Tool</th><th>ID</th><th>Status</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Google Analytics 4</td><td>G-XGFPCV10CX</td><td>Loaded in root layout</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Google Tag Manager</td><td>GTM-KB7M5KBL</td><td>Loaded in root layout</td></tr>
</table>

<p>SPA page views tracked via <code>usePageView</code> on Works, Blog, and detail pages.
Engagement events cover case study clicks, blog clicks, outbound project links, and contact actions.</p>

<h2>11. Scoring Snapshot</h2>

<table>
  <tr><th>Category</th><th>Score (1–10)</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Technical metadata</td><td>9</td><td>Strong titles, descriptions, canonicals, OG/Twitter</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Crawlability</td><td>9</td><td>robots + sitemap + MDX URLs</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Structured data</td><td>8</td><td>Person/WebSite/Article/CreativeWork</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Content depth</td><td>6</td><td>4 case studies + 2 posts</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Social sharing assets</td><td>6</td><td>Custom post images; project OG not 1200×630-optimized</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Internal linking</td><td>7</td><td>Home → works/blog; case-study cards highlighted</td></tr>
</table>

<p><strong>Overall: ~8/10 technical SEO</strong> for a personal portfolio. Content volume is the main limiter.</p>

<h2>12. Risks &amp; Gaps</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Thin content surface vs many external-only projects.</li>
  <li>Default OG image may not be ideal 1200×630 for LinkedIn/Twitter.</li>
  <li>No BreadcrumbList / ItemList yet.</li>
  <li>Possible GA + GTM double-counting if GTM also loads GA — verify config.</li>
  <li>Raw script tags for GA (Next prefers next/script) — hygiene, not SEO-blocking.</li>
</ol>

<h2>13. Recommended Next Actions</h2>

<h3>High priority</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Submit sitemap in Google Search Console.</li>
  <li>Request indexing for new /works/* and /blog/* URLs after publish.</li>
  <li>Add more MDX case studies for top projects.</li>
  <li>Publish 1–2 blog posts per month.</li>
</ol>

<h3>Medium priority</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Create dedicated 1200×630 OG images per case study and post.</li>
  <li>Add BreadcrumbList JSON-LD to detail pages.</li>
  <li>Add ItemList JSON-LD to /works and /blog.</li>
  <li>Add datePublished / dateModified to project frontmatter.</li>
</ol>

<h3>Lower priority</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Migrate GA/GTM to next/script.</li>
  <li>Validate JSON-LD with Google Rich Results Test.</li>
  <li>Audit LinkedIn share previews with Post Inspector.</li>
</ol>

<h2>14. SEO File Map</h2>
<pre>
src/app/layout.tsx
src/app/sitemap.ts
src/app/robots.ts
src/app/*/layout.tsx
src/app/works/[id]/layout.tsx + page.tsx
src/app/blog/[slug]/layout.tsx + page.tsx
src/lib/site.ts
src/lib/project.ts / project-seo.ts
src/lib/blog.ts / blog-seo.ts
src/lib/gtag.ts
content/projects/*.mdx
content/blogs/*.mdx
</pre>

<h2>15. Conclusion</h2>

<p>Your portfolio SEO setup is <strong>production-ready</strong> for App Router: absolute canonicals,
social metadata on dynamic MDX pages, correct sitemap/robots, and Person + WebSite + Article + CreativeWork
structured data.</p>

<p>The biggest opportunity is <strong>more indexable content</strong> (additional case studies and blog posts),
followed by dedicated social images and Breadcrumb/ItemList schema.</p>

